icity of the root $x=-2$ is $2,$ which is even, the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=0$ is $1,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=0$ is a simple root, the graph must *not* be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Since the multiplicity of the root $x=2$ is $3,$ which is odd, the graph must cross the $x$-axis at this point. Moreover, because $x=2$ is a triple-root, the graph must be tangent to the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nOnly the graphs $\\text{I}$ and $\\text{IV}$ satisfy these conditions.\n\nTo choose between these two graphs, we need to consider the end behavior. Since the leading coefficient is negative, as $x$ approaches $\\infty ,$ $y$ approaches $-\\infty .$ Since only graph $\\text{I}$ displays this end behavior, the correct answer is $\\text{I}.$" 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250008 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250009 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250010 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250011 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250012 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1041 "selection" 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250009 13194139533769 true] [17592186250007 1110 #uuid "15d33e1f-9e7a-53d0-9138-93ebb23cfe48" 13194139533769 true] [17592186250008 1034 "\\text{II}" 13194139533769 true] [17592186250008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533769 true] [17592186250008 1111 #uuid "7aaf244d-f2b0-591f-897a-52065342a0be" 13194139533769 true] [17592186250009 1034 "\\text{I}" 13194139533769 true] [17592186250009 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533769 true] [17592186250009 1111 #uuid "c084bf6e-084e-5644-9745-dd6f1dc747e6" 13194139533769 true] [17592186250010 1034 "\\text{III}" 13194139533769 true] 